  "statement": "You have an array of floating point numbers `averages` which is initially empty. You are given an array `nums` of `n` integers where `n` is even.\n\nYou repeat the following procedure `n / 2` times:\n\n*   Remove the **smallest** element, `minElement`, and the **largest** element `maxElement`, from `nums`.\n*   Add `(minElement + maxElement) / 2` to `averages`.\n\nReturn the **minimum** element in `averages`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** nums = \\[7,8,3,4,15,13,4,1\\]\n\n**Output:** 5.5\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nstep\n\nnums\n\naverages\n\n0\n\n\\[7,8,3,4,15,13,4,1\\]\n\n\\[\\]\n\n1\n\n\\[7,8,3,4,13,4\\]\n\n\\[8\\]\n\n2\n\n\\[7,8,4,4\\]\n\n\\[8,8\\]\n\n3\n\n\\[7,4\\]\n\n\\[8,8,6\\]\n\n4\n\n\\[\\]\n\n\\[8,8,6,5.5\\]\n\nThe smallest element of averages, 5.5, is returned.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** nums = \\[1,9,8,3,10,5\\]\n\n**Output:** 5.5\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nstep\n\nnums\n\naverages\n\n0\n\n\\[1,9,8,3,10,5\\]\n\n\\[\\]\n\n1\n\n\\[9,8,3,5\\]\n\n\\[5.5\\]\n\n2\n\n\\[8,5\\]\n\n\\[5.5,6\\]\n\n3\n\n\\[\\]\n\n\\[5.5,6,6.5\\]\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n**Input:** nums = \\[1,2,3,7,8,9\\]\n\n**Output:** 5.0\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nstep\n\nnums\n\naverages\n\n0\n\n\\[1,2,3,7,8,9\\]\n\n\\[\\]\n\n1\n\n\\[2,3,7,8\\]\n\n\\[5\\]\n\n2\n\n\\[3,7\\]\n\n\\[5,5\\]\n\n3\n\n\\[\\]\n\n\\[5,5,5\\]\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `2 <= n == nums.length <= 50`\n*   `n` is even.\n*   `1 <= nums[i] <= 50`",
  "constraints": [
    "2 <= n == nums.length <= 50",
    "n is even.",
    "1 <= nums[i] <= 50"
  ],
